EXACT_EDIT 'Both compositions follow by multiplication in the free relation\nmodule. The quotient is therefore $\\mathbb Z/b$, sending $s$' -> 'These formulas identify the actual relation sublattices.\nOn the four-column source the primitive syzygy is\n$v_0=(r,n,-m,0)^t$. Let $A$ express the three $E$ columns\nin the four $C_1,C_2,C_3,G_e$ columns, and let $B$ express\nthose four columns in the $E$ coordinates as displayed.\nThen $BA=I_3$ and\n$AB=I_4-\\sigma v_0(0,1,e,0)$.\nThus they are inverse maps between $\\mathbb Z^3$ and\n$\\mathbb Z^4/\\mathbb Zv_0$; $v_0$ is primitive since\n$\\gcd(m,n)=1$. The quotient in the ambient cycle module is\ntherefore $\\mathbb Z/b$, sending $s$'
PRESENTATION_MAP sigma -1 BA=I3; AB=I4-sigma*(r,n,-m,0)^t*(0,1,e,0) PASS
